    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP, today\u2019s slate centers on exploiting vulnerable arms to chase volume and stolen base opportunities. **Corbin Carroll** (83.08) is our highest-rated asset, benefiting from a prime spot in the two-hole against Kumar Rocker. His efficiency score is bolstered by a favorable matchup and a slow delivery profile from the opposing pitcher, which significantly elevates his theft probability. **Mickey Moniak** (75.42) and **Josh Naylor** (75.64) round out our premier tier; **Mickey Moniak** receives a massive +14% lift from his platoon advantage against Mitch Keller, while **Josh Naylor** is locked in as a priority start at the UTIL spot thanks to a +19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable projected lineup position in the heart of the order.\n\nTactical adjustments remain key, particularly with the bottom of our lineup. **Henry Bolte** (65.39) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.19) are strong plays today, as both receive a notable +10% boost from favorable park factors against Matthew Liberatore. **James Wood** (71.31) also presents a high floor, as the wind-out conditions and an ideal leadoff role mitigate the risks posed by Nick Lodolo\u2019s arsenal. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (60.42); while he crossed the \"Strong\" threshold, his score suffered a sharp -15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter, ultimately leading the optimizer to prefer the higher ceiling provided by **Josh Naylor**. \n\nRegarding risk management, note that several positions\u2014specifically **Dalton Rushing**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2014remain \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have projected their placements based on historical usage, any late-scratch or order drop could necessitate a recalibration of their efficiency scores. Additionally, while we are leaning into speed where possible, **Brice Turang** faces an elite hold pitcher in Michael King, creating a slight drag on his theft upside. We are comfortably sitting **Travis Bazzana** (31.09) and **Zach McKinstry** (38.26) to preserve our game caps, as both currently fall well below our 40-point efficiency floor.",
